NewMod change log
=================

2026-11-28 — Arena.ai Agent Mode
--------------------------------
Multi-architecture / cross-platform builds and dedicated-server compatibility
* Makefile and tools/lipo_universal.py: support Linux x86_64 and i386
  (<mod>.mp.x86_64.so, <mod>.mp.i386.so), Windows x64 and x86 (<mod>_mp_x64.dll,
  <mod>_mp_x86.dll), and macOS universal x86_64 + arm64 (<mod>_mac) matching
  ET: Legacy's Sys_GetDLLName conventions. Target glibc 2.17 on cross-compiled
  Linux modules, pack client modules into build/overzealous-all.pk3, and add
  server-dist (build/overzealous-server-linux.tar.gz) with loose 32-bit and
  64-bit qagame server modules alongside overzealous-all.pk3.
* src/game/q_shared.h, g_main.c, g_syscalls.c, cgame/cg_main.c, cg_syscalls.c,
  ui/ui_main.c, ui/ui_syscalls.c: add DLLEXPORT + QDECL on vmMain and dllEntry
  so Windows 32/64-bit PE DLLs export exact unmangled entrypoints; normalize
  _WIN32/WIN32, __APPLE__/MACOS_X, portable SinCos, and 64-bit pointer-offset
  casts across x86_64, arm64, and _WIN64.
* src/game/g_crash.c and src/cgame/cg_crash.c: support i386, x86_64, and
  aarch64 Linux crash instruction pointers, typed POSIX signal/ELF casts under
  C++, and 32-bit-only guards around legacy Win32 imagehlp backtraces.
* src/game/g_main.c (ServerCheck) and g_client.c (CGAMEFileExists): allow
  custom non-etmain fs_game directories (e.g., ozmod or overzealous), recognize
  overzealous*.pk3 in sv_pakNames, and fail cleanly via G_Error instead of
  terminating the host process with exit(1).
* Omnibot/Common/BotLoadLibrary.cpp: add 64-bit omnibot_et.x86_64.so and
  omnibot_et_x64.dll fallback library names.

2026-11-21 — Arena.ai Agent Mode
--------------------------------
NewMod is derived directly from No Quarter by the No Quarter Mod Team and
contributors, using the baseline and other inspected projects recorded in
PROVENANCE.md. These are development changes, not a claim of complete
Jaymod/Oz feature equivalence or release readiness.

Build, identity and native integration
* Added Makefile and .gitignore for Linux x86-64 ET: Legacy native game,
  cgame and UI modules, separate Lua/Omni-Bot/optional NQ-key build variants,
  and test targets. Reject empty, multiple or invalid feature values and
  unsupported architecture labels. Bundled the Lua 5.1.4 interpreter source
  from the inspected Jaymod snapshot; no ET: Legacy engine or game media is
  bundled.
* src/game/g_local.h and bg_public.h: distinguish NewMod directory and
  advertised game/version strings; retain NQ's compatibility constant. Added
  state and declarations needed by the command adapters and match sentinel.
* src/game/nm_syscall.h and game/g_syscalls.c, cgame/cg_syscalls.c,
  ui/ui_syscalls.c: use pointer-width native syscall arguments and the ET:
  Legacy varargs terminator. game/g_main.c, cgame/cg_main.c and ui/ui_main.c
  use pointer-width native VM entrypoints. Selected 2.86.2 ABI values/layouts
  and calls are regression-tested; the complete ABI is not proven.
* game/g_main.c: require a distinct newmod directory and keep the inherited
  engine-version checks and NQ media warnings; do not advertise an unverified
  project URL. Make the config filename parameter read-only.
* game/g_match_tokens.c: emit needed lookup symbols with modern C inline
  semantics. game/g_crash.c and cgame/cg_crash.c: avoid redefining a GNU
  feature macro. cgame/cg_local.h: avoid a libc CHAR_WIDTH collision.

Selected Oz/Jaymod-inspired behavior
* game/g_shrubbot.c and g_shrubbot.h: register putteam/lol aliases, giba,
  flinga/throwa/launcha, panzerwar/sniperwar/riflewar, spec and report,
  with NQ permission and relevant target/tyranny checks. War commands operate
  on NQ's existing bits; mass actions protect higher and immutable targets.
* Added game/g_newmod.c and declarations in g_shrubbot.h: crazygravity,
  shake, splat, splata, smite, firegod, news, about, status, lsplayers,
  spree and tspree. They use NQ state and are adaptations rather than full
  upstream subsystems. News validates the filename, sound capacity and entity
  reserve. !firegod is adapted from Oz: it toggles a target's flaming god
  mode, granting invulnerability for the NQ burn duration on a new fire and
  restoring mortal damage on a repeat, with optional noclip. It is not Oz's
  separate firegod timer model.
* game/g_main.c and g_local.h: schedule and restore saved gravity; game/
  g_active.c schedules connection-local targeted shake. game/g_combat.c and
  g_local.h add a splat-only damage flag that bypasses spawn invulnerability
  while retaining other protection gates. Existing non-splat damage behavior
  is not globally switched to bypass spawn protection.
* game/g_main.c, g_cmds.c, g_shrubbot.c and g_local.h: private report routing,
  dedicated report-file and admin-level cvars, sanitization and per-connection
  limits. Reports are intercepted before module chat/log/Lua dispatch, but
  engine debug logs or server-side demos can record raw input earlier.
* game/g_newmod.c, g_shrubbot.c and g_shrubbot.h: add NQ-backed stats, ftime,
  chicken, crybaby, banlist, baninfo, levlist, levinfo, userinfo, userlist,
  page and seen. Pages rebuild live data with permission checks; !seen retains
  a bounded map-local history only for visible NQ admin records, including
  GUID lookup keys and names in memory. Neither is Jaymod database parity.
* game/g_newmod.c, g_shrubbot.c, g_cmds.c, g_client.c, g_main.c and
  cgame/cg_consolecmds.c: add bounded connection-local !warn/!dewarn and
  /warnings, with permission, hierarchy, sanitization and lifecycle checks.
  This is not Oz's persistent, expiring, auto-punishing warning store. Normal
  chat, admin logs, engine logs, demos or plugins can retain the command text.
* game/g_combat.c and g_newmod.c: add !spreerecord with an NQ-derived,
  map-local high watermark updated on enemy-kill streaks during play. It
  retains a name snapshot until map initialization; it is not Oz's durable
  per-map/overall records or eligibility rules. cgame/cg_consolecmds.c and
  game/g_cmds.c add the narrower /knives count command.
* game/g_newmod.c and g_shrubbot.c: add Oz-inspired !spawn with flag % and
  tyranny. It uses NQ reinforcement only on eligible limbo players and
  respects hierarchy, immutability, pause and match-phase checks. It skips
  wave and respawn/death-animation waits; it is not Oz's direct respawn.
* game/bg_public.h, bg_misc.c, bg_pmove.c, bg_weapons.c, g_weapon.c,
  g_client.c, g_items.c, g_active.c and g_cmds.c, plus cgame/cg_consolecmds.c,
  cg_event.c, cg_playerstate.c, cg_predict.c, cg_snapshot.c and cg_weapons.c:
  implement opt-in Jaymod-inspired teammate adrenaline weapon ID 63 and a
  separate Oz-inspired /adrenother command. NewMod g_medics bits 8192 and
  16384 avoid upstream bit conflicts with NQ. The share tool reuses NQ's
  self-adrenaline pool and media names; it is not Jaymod parity. Movement
  fire-event tagging affects other weapons even when it is disabled, so
  matching NewMod client and server builds are mandatory. Real multiplayer,
  correction behavior, bot translation, demos and authorized media remain
  unverified; no other Jaymod/Oz-only weapons are implemented here.

Boundary, portability and safety fixes
* game/g_cmds.c, g_client.c, g_shrubbot.c, g_svcmds.c and g_lua.c: reserve
  MAX_CLIENTS+1 integers for lists with a -1 terminator. Match numeric slots
  without interpreting an empty or overflowed number as a valid slot.
* game/g_cmds.c: fix Q_SayArgc/Q_SayArgv/Q_SayConcatArgs stepping beyond the
  static argument buffer's terminating NUL after multiple trailing spaces;
  consistently handle repeated spaces and reject missing trailing arguments.
  game/g_shrubbot.c: replace control bytes in formatted admin-log entries and
  ensure one terminating newline even when the entry is truncated. This does
  not redact logged arguments or sanitize engine/chat logs.
* game/q_shared.c: replace Q_StrReplace with bounded, empty-safe substitution;
  game/g_cmds.c clears stale shortcut values. game/g_shrubbot.c bounds custom
  command expansion and rejects unsafe player substitutions, malformed UTF-8,
  ambiguous comment/quote contexts and oversized results. Trusted templates
  can still execute privileged console commands without nested permission
  checks; ET: Legacy sanitizes some client text before module dispatch.
* game/q_shared.c and q_shared.h: bound quoted and unquoted COM_ParseExt
  tokens, stop at EOF without advancing beyond it, report malformed quotes or
  block comments, and treat UTF-8 bytes as token bytes. This shared change can
  affect game/cgame/UI asset parsing; broad compatibility remains unverified.
* game/g_shrubbot.c, g_shrubbot.h, g_local.h and g_client.c: reserve NULL
  sentinels in all dense shrub lists, bound and validate custom command levels,
  stage reloads before replacing live records and reject malformed/oversized
  config input (32 MiB limit). Handle missing/failed reads without discarding
  a prior snapshot; disabled sections cannot modify preceding records.
  Quote/sanitize written data fields, preserve representable trusted templates
  and refuse unsafe template serialization before opening the file. Disk writes
  remain non-atomic and are not fully checked. Match active mute records by
  nonempty GUID, restore them after renames, and reconcile purely shrub-owned
  mutes after successful reload; combined sources remain conservative. GUIDs
  are not authentication, and the single-timer model remains limited.
* game/g_utils.c: terminate the fallback campaign map/devmap command with a
  newline so an appended console command cannot run into it.
* game/g_active.c and g_shrubbot.c: widen adrenaline deadline/cooldown and
  purchase comparisons, and avoid spectator/limbo follower state corruption.
  These changes affect inherited adrenaline handling even with share disabled;
  synthetic edge tests are not a complete game-clock or multiplayer audit.
* game/g_shrubbot.c: harden the inherited ban-creation handlers. Ban
  durations multiplied by a week/day/hour/minute modifier now saturate the
  32-bit product and the persisted epoch expiry instead of overflowing them;
  offline `!banguid` records require exactly PB_GUID_LENGTH characters;
  offline `!banIP` records accept only well-formed IPv4 addresses (no
  leading zeros, octets 0-255, exactly four octets) so an arbitrary short
  string cannot match every address containing it; temporary bans reject
  non-positive durations; and IP stripping is bounded. This does not make
  GUIDs or IPs authentication.
* game/g_shrubbot.c: parse shrubbot flag strings with a bounded walk that
  honors NQ's `-denial+resumed` syntax and wildcard-exclusion suffixes without
  walking past a trailing delimiter or the terminating NUL. Empty, `unknown`,
  `NO_GUID` and `offline` keys still cannot match admin or mute records.
  This is a permission-lookup fix, not an authentication fix.
* game/q_math.c: fix LP64 float-bit conversion and zero-vector normalization.
  game/q_shared.c: bound the two-word bit helpers and va formatting;
  game/bg_animation.c: initialize the complete two-word animation result.
* game/g_team.c and cgame/cg_main.c: allocate and validate full 64-player
  team-info packets, reject short/invalid entries before mutation and avoid
  unaligned access while retaining NQ's native-endian wire representation.
  game/g_main.c validates the server packet envelope and optional key/system
  payload sizes. cgame/cg_main.c initializes optional system-info header
  padding and writes its integer with memcpy.
* cgame/cg_uid.c: bound and terminate the inherited NQ key file/packet,
  initialize packet padding, remove key debug output, and avoid using a
  shared fallback if the key file cannot be opened for writing. The engine
  API does not report short writes. The inherited identity remains
  spoofable, is not authentication and is disabled by default.
* game/g_session.c: use bounded, writable storage when reading a saved NQ
  GUID, including builds without AUTO_GUID. game/g_xpsave.c: reject unsafe
  GUID path components and overlong paths for normal and optional NQ saves.
* game/g_main.c, g_cmds.c, g_client.c, g_svcmds.c, g_lua.c,
  cgame/cg_servercmds.c and cg_info.c: repair selected data-as-format calls,
  bound bindsearch assembly, terminate long log lines, and avoid raw userinfo
  logging. This is a targeted, not a complete, format or privacy audit.
* game/g_lua.c and g_lua.h: use bundled headers, pointer-width entity fields,
  record field capacities and check selected entity/client/array/VM indices,
  item and string handling. Bound Lua filesystem reads and writes, preserve
  binary strings, and use Lua-owned zero-initialized read storage. Engine
  reads do not return an actual byte count. Consume callback return values
  and error objects so repeated hooks do not accumulate stack entries. Skip
  empty module-list entries, check allocations and free rejected module code.
* game/g_sha1.c, g_local.h and g_lua.c: compute module allowlist fingerprints
  over the full file length, including binary NUL bytes, while retaining the
  string hash helper. Existing allowlist entries for affected bytecode may
  need updating. SHA-1 is not proof of trust; Lua remains unsandboxed and the
  entire Lua interface has not been audited.
* cgame/cg_debriefing.c and ui/ui_shared.c: test characters instead of
  pointer addresses and bound edit-field paint offsets. cgame/cg_players.c:
  copy the entire ladder torso axis. game/g_etbot_interface.cpp: map the
  Johnson scoped weapon to its game weapon bit, not its Omni-Bot ID.

Tests, documentation and retained terms
* Added tests/ fake-engine, native ABI, UI, command, permission, report,
  gravity lifecycle, real damage/death, 64-player/malformed packet, XP path,
  optional NQ-key, invalid build options, Lua hook stack/allowlist and
  Omni-Bot regressions. Added an optional ET: Legacy dedicated-server smoke
  harness that generates disposable synthetic stand-ins and checks Lua,
  commands, gravity restoration and map restart, with an optional timed
  gravity test. Added tests for weapon item order, Pmove-produced fire and
  binocular events, prediction correction, spectators, imported command
  privacy, warning lifecycle, chat argument parsing, and death-handler spree
  updates. The populated warning/seen map-init fixture interrupts at the first
  engine print. Added game/cgame/UI parser boundary and full shrub config
  read/write/reload tests, including exact capacities, malformed ACLs, hostile
  data and mute lifecycle. A separate ET: Legacy fixture compiles a synthetic
  bot-protocol stub and checks client-command, pause/spawn, custom reload/write,
  mute, warning, death, disconnect and restart paths using placeholder assets.
  The bot smoke also exercises actual mute/unmute records and their
  restoration across a reload. Added fake-engine tests for the actual
  `!firegod` toggle (god-mode, timer, noclip and target eligibility) and for
  the ban-creation handlers (duration saturation, GUID length, IPv4
  validation, temporary-ban duration and host/bot/hierarchy rejection).
  Neither it nor the no-client smoke is real Omni-Bot or a network client.
  Tests do not replace real client, download, demo or multiplayer validation.
* Added tools/import_inventory.py and docs/import-inventory.md for a pinned,
  preprocessor-independent name/ID inventory with parser tests. The scan can
  omit dynamic and other dispatch surfaces and does not establish parity.
* Added README.md, PROVENANCE.md, LEGAL, CONTRIB and licenses/ copies/notices;
  the original NQ license, source notices and asset restrictions remain
  applicable and require further deployment/distribution review.
